e desire for embrace, having desirable beauty, / having rounded soft breasts, having creeper-like tresses, / how can I forget and remain still? I indeed, there, / like a shivering-headed calf of a good cow with abundant milk-flow, / with the desire to see its mother, / she of dark beauty looked with a languishing gaze.","translation":"She has an intense desire to embrace, and desirable beauty. She has rounded, soft breasts and creeper-like tresses. How can I forget her and remain at peace? Like a shivering-headed calf of a good cow with a heavy flow of milk, longing to see its mother, that dark-complexioned beautiful woman looked at me with a languishing, tender gaze.","modern":"தழுவிக் கொள்ளும் பேராவல் கொண்டவள்; விரும்பத்தக்க அழகுடையவள்; திரண்ட மென்மையான மார்பகங்களையும் கொடி போன்ற கூந்தலையும் உடையவள். அவளை மறந்து நான் எவ்வாறு அமைதியாக இருக்க முடியும்? மடி நிறைந்த நல்ல பசுவின் நடுக்கமுறும் தலையையுடைய கன்று தன் தாயைக் காண விரும்பும் ஏக்கம் போன்ற ஏக்கத்துடன், அந்த மாநிறத்து அழகி என்னை மென்மையாகப் பார்த்தாளே!","explanation":"The hero is speaking to himself, recalling the intense love and parting look of his beloved. He describes her physical beauty—her soft rounded breasts, her long creeper-like hair—and her deep desire to embrace him, wondering how he could ever forget her. He vividly recalls her parting gaze, comparing her longing look to that of a trembling newborn calf yearning to see its mother, a cow with full udders. This poem belongs to the Kuriñci tiṇai, which is associated with the union of lovers and the deep longing of separation. The simile of the shivering calf beautifully captures the vulnerability, innocence, and intense longing of the heroine when the hero departs. Key words include 'கவவு' (embrace), 'சாஅய் நோக்கினளே' (she looked with a languishing gaze), and 'மாஅயோளே' (the dark-complexioned beautiful woman).","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.6],[0.6,1.2],[1.2,1.8],[1.8,2.3],[2.3,3.4],[3.4,3.74],[3.74,4.2],[4.2,4.4],[4.81,5.62],[5.6